WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.840
There are few things more upsetting&nbsp;
than the idea of a lonely death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:09.040
To pass off the mortal coil without anyone around&nbsp;
you, anyone to comfort you in your final moments.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:14.320
Thankfully, SCP-4999 exists to&nbsp;
help solve this tragic issue.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:20.480
SCP-4999 is a humanoid who appears dressed in dark&nbsp;
formalwear. He manifests at the side of fatally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.200
injured, critically ill, or otherwise dying people&nbsp;
within the last twenty minutes of their life.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.160
He will only appear to those dying alone, sitting&nbsp;
or standing with them if no chair is available in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:34.880
an act of what seems like silent respect. Next,&nbsp;
he will pull out two cigarettes: One for himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.200
and one for his dying friend. He’ll then hold&nbsp;
their hand, place a hand on their shoulder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.880
or engage in some other kind of comforting&nbsp;
physical touch in their final moments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:47.360
then disappear shortly after the person has&nbsp;
passed, leaving no trace that he was ever there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.440
except for the left behind cigarette.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:53.600
While no one is exactly sure what he is&nbsp;
or why he has chosen to keep his vigil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.840
thanks to SCP-4999, nobody ever really dies alone.

